{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the stuck `orders-validator` consumer and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned status 200 with the message \"Submission received\".\n\n- **Cause:** a malformed, non-JSON record at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` Kafka topic made `orders-validator` pause that partition and never move on. Every later order was blocked behind it.\n- **Fix:** I edited `consumer.py` in the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap. The consumer now logs the bad record, commits its offset and continues. I then restarted the `orders-validator` deployment.\n- **Result:** the consumer is processing again. Its logs showed committed offset 50 after the restart, and the new records were being processed.\n\nI didn't check frontend or checkout latency. I only confirmed that the pipeline is flowing again and that the other pods were running.\n\nI didn't look into where the malformed record came from. Skipped records are only logged, not sent to a dead-letter topic."}}
